  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return grid\n    \n    H = len(grid)\n    W = len(grid[0])\n    \n    mid_r = H // 2\n    mid_c = W // 2\n    \n    r_max_top = -1\n    r_min_bottom = H\n    c_max_left = -1\n    c_min_right = W\n    \n    # Find the boundaries of patterns in each half\n    for r in range(H):\n        for c in range(W):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                if r < mid_r:\n                    r_max_top = max(r_max_top, r)\n                else:\n                    r_min_bottom = min(r_min_bottom, r)\n                \n                if c < mid_c:\n                    c_max_left = max(c_max_left, c)\n                else:\n                    c_min_right = min(c_min_right, c)\n    \n    # Calculate shift amounts\n    v_shift = 0\n    if r_max_top >= 0 and r_min_bottom < H:\n        v_shift = (r_min_bottom - r_max_top - 1) // 2\n    \n    h_shift = 0\n    if c_max_left >= 0 and c_min_right < W:\n        h_shift = (c_min_right - c_max_left - 1) // 2\n    \n    # Create output grid\n    output = [[0 for _ in range(W)] for _ in range(H)]\n    \n    # Apply transformations\n    for r in range(H):\n        for c in range(W):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                # Determine new row\n                if r < mid_r:\n                    new_r = r + v_shift\n                else:\n                    new_r = r - v_shift\n                \n                # Determine new column\n                if c < mid_c:\n                    new_c = c + h_shift\n                else:\n                    new_c = c - h_shift\n                \n                # Place in output if within bounds\n                if 0 <= new_r < H and 0 <= new_c < W:\n                    output[new_r][new_c] = grid[r][c]\n    \n    return output\n```",
